{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Closure status (2026-08-22): all 10 stories are implemented and MERGED. The only thing blocking `transition open -> ... -> closed` is obtaining a SIGNED plan-review PASS, which is failing for an infra/concurrency reason EXTERNAL to this epic's scope -- not a plan or code gap.\n\nreview-plan on this epic computes PASS (0 blocking, 5 advisory) and emits the sidecar, but signing exhausts its 3-attempt retry budget under concurrent multi-session load. Confirmed mechanism (read-only reproduction, 12 trials, no LLM): the sign freshness fence wraps a ~10s collect() (this epic has many plan-material pins -> bug 3d57-602f-0b75-48ee's O(pins) full-store reduction), and foreground ticket writes from other sessions move tracker HEAD within that window -> before != after -> ~25% of attempts exhaust and persist no attestation. reason histogram {'head-move': 12}; 0 enrich-drain commits (churn is foreground). This is bug a83f-6348-a08c-401d (sign fence compares store-wide HEAD, not subject generation), amplified by 3d57 (collect window length); see my comments on both.\n\nPaths to close WITHOUT --force: (a) land a83f or 3d57 (either shortens/removes the fence failure), then sign; or (b) opportunistically re-run review-plan in a calmer window -- 75% of single attempts already land a stable ~10s window -- via the cached-sidecar replay (no new LLM spend). --force will not be used."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787440056725957001,"uuid":"8024f6d8-aa5a-4da1-b4e7-7238ad35f23b"}